class.description:
[NetwRingBuffer] rounds its capacity up to a power of two so [method record], [method get_at], and [method bracketing_ticks] can stay cheap in interpolation and rollback hot paths: a capacity that is a power of two wraps an index with a mask rather than a modulo, and that is the whole reason this type exists rather than an [Array].
[codeblock]
var history := NetwRingBuffer.create(32)
history.record(tick, snapshot)
var exact := history.get_at(tick)
var pair := history.bracketing_ticks(render_tick)
[/codeblock]
